      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Ridiculous honestly. The game is basically unplayable on Quest 3S. I've been having this issue since the last update.\n\n1. Open VRC\n\n2. Visit any world\n\n3. Clear Preload on home world\n\n4. Go home\n\n5. Clear Preload on previous world\n\n6. Hit \"Clear Content Cache\" (which does nothing)\n\n7. A box pops up that says \"3.72Gb will be cleared on restart\"\n\n8. Close game from Quest or in-game menu\n\n9. Reopen game\n\n10. Sitting at 3.72Gb content cache\n\nThe Quest 3/ 3S can only handle 4Gb before it starts running into errors and crashing, which means I can't go anywhere or do anything for very long at all. I have uninstalled and reinstalled the game, which fixed nothing. It just climbed back up to 3Gb in one night.\n\nI have tried removing prints, stickers, emojis and photos. I have tried removing avatars. I have tried keeping people's avatars off. I have tried only visiting one world aside from my home world. I have reset my WiFi. I have messed with my WiFi settings, toggling between IPv4 and IPv6. I have tried every trick I can think of.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
